<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Casimir I of Kuyavia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1211–<a href="/years/1267">1267</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Casimir I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuyavia">Kuyavia</a> was a Piast duke, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konrad-i-of-masovia">Konrad I of Masovia</a>, who received Kuyavia in 1233 and Łęczyca after his father's death in 1247. He fought his neighbours and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> and border lands. His sons, including Władysław I the Elbow-high, divided his duchies, and Władysław later reunited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/casimir-i-of-kuyavia.jpg" alt="Casimir I of Kuyavia" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maksymilian Fajans · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kazimierz_I_kujawski.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
